---
description: Backend / data / auth conventions
globs:
  - "app/api/**"
  - "app/actions/**"
  - "lib/**"
  - "src/lib/**"
  - "supabase/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Backend rules - HITSHCM

- Validate inputs at the boundary (server actions / route handlers).
- Enforce auth on sensitive operations; assume deny-by-default.
- Prefer server-side Supabase client for privileged operations; never expose service-role keys to the client.
- Keep business rules documented when non-obvious; add ADR if the data model changes.
- Migrations / schema changes should be explicit and minimal for the current slice.
- Log safely: no secrets, no full PII dumps.
